          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Whey can be kosher, but only when an agency certifies the finished powder, because whey comes from cheesemaking and kosher law has rules on cheese production. Kosher whey is always dairy, usually marked OU-D or with a D beside another symbol. You cannot tell from the ingredient list whether a whey is kosher."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What does OU-D mean on protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
