          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is there a pareve protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Plant proteins such as pea and rice, and egg white, can be certified pareve, meaning neither meat nor dairy. The finished powder still needs certification, because flavors and shared whey equipment can make it dairy or DE. Check the symbol on the tub; a plant ingredient list alone does not prove pareve status."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I drink a whey protein shake after eating meat?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "If you keep kosher and wait between meat and dairy, a whey shake counts as dairy, so you would wait your community's customary time, often six hours. A certified pareve plant or egg white powder avoids the wait. Customs vary, so follow your own practice or ask your rabbi."
